  "scope": "The released EffectRequest decoder delegates closed current-operation and legacy-query envelopes to leselang-command. The VM keeps its public fields, serialization, original ContinuationImage and complete post-decode validation. The VM-free captured source/successor fixture now uses the same canonical envelope codec with numeric-token frames before unchanged native admission. A frozen original decoder compares 74 valid current/legacy forms, 1332 malformed/duplicate/mixed/missing/nested/trailing/truncated inputs and 592 semantic admission failures with identical canonical bytes or exact error strings. Direct adapter tests retain move-only native continuations, borrowed JSON lifetimes and absent deadline behavior without adding Clone/Debug/Serialize requirements. Decoded data intentionally does not certify identity, semantic budgets, source/frame provenance, live authority or replay permission. Input bounds and stream framing/end checks remain with ingress owners; the released VM still refuses trailing input through its normal whole-input serde entry. Memory-only and default SQLite/reference suites pass. The native export remains product-free and does not include this product codec. No language, evaluator, meter, wire/journal schema or extraction-completion change is claimed.",
